________________________________________
Common Mistakes
•	Thinking packets travel in a straight line.
•	Assuming the Internet is owned by one company.
•	Believing every packet always follows the same route.
•	Confusing routers with switches.
________________________________________
Memory Tips
NIC
The network door of your computer.
Router
Chooses the next road.
ISP
Connects your local network to the Internet.
Routing
Choosing the best available path.
Redundancy
Having backup routes when something fails.
