Real-World Case Study
Problem: Employees in a company reported that the company website was loading very slowly.
Investigation:
The network engineer checked:
1.	DNS resolution
2.	Internet connectivity
3.	Router performance
4.	Server response time
The problem turned out to be an overloaded web server.
Solution:
The company added additional servers and distributed traffic using a load balancer.
Result:
Page loading times improved significantly.
